prime factorization of 24:\n\n\\[\n24 = 2^3 \\times 3^1\n\\]\n\nNext, we use the prime factorization to determine the number of positive divisors. If a number \\( n \\) has a prime factorization of \\( p_1^{e_1} \\times p_2^{e_2} \\times \\cdots \\times p_k^{e_k} \\), then the number of positive divisors of \\( n \\) is given by:\n\n\\[\n(e_1 + 1)(e_2 + 1) \\cdots (e_k + 1)\n\\]\n\nFor \\( 24 = 2^3 \\times 3^1 \\):\n\n\\[\n(e_1 + 1) = (3 + 1) = 4\n\\]\n\\[\n(e_2 + 1) = (1 + 1) = 2\n\\]\n\nThus, the total number of positive divisors of 24 is:\n\n\\[\n4 \\times 2 = 8\n\\]\n\nWe list all the positive divisors of 24 to confirm:\n\n\\[\n1, 2, 3, 4, 6, 8, 12, 24\n\\]\n\nThere are 8 positive divisors. Therefore, there are 8 positive integers \\( t \\) that will make the expression \\(\\frac{24}{t}\\) an integer.\n\nThe final answer is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{8}\n\\]"},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{8}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true},"id":"number_theory:215"}
